{
  "title": "54: al-Qamar القمر",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ وَانْشَقَّ الْقَمَرُ‏(1)\n\nThe Hour has drawn near and the moon is split.\nوَاِنْ يَّرَوْا اٰيَةً يُّعْرِضُوْا وَيَقُوْلُوْا سِحْرٌ مُّسْتَمِرٌّ‏(2)\n\nIf they see a sign, they turn away, and say, ‘An incessant magic!’\nوَكَذَّبُوْا وَاتَّبَعُوْۤا اَهْوَآءَهُمْ‌ وَكُلُّ اَمْرٍ مُّسْتَقِرٌّ‏(3)\n\nThey denied and followed their own desires, and every matter has a setting [appropriate to it].\nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ مِّنَ الْاَنْۢبَآءِ مَا فِيْهِ مُزْدَجَرٌۙ‏(4)\n\nThere have already come to them reports containing admonishment,\nحِكْمَةٌۢ بَالِغَةٌ‌ فَمَا تُغْنِ النُّذُرُۙ‏(5)\n\n[and representing] far-reaching wisdom; but warnings are of no avail!\nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ‌ۘ يَوْمَ يَدْعُ الدَّاعِ اِلٰى شَىْءٍ نُّكُرٍۙ‏(6)\n\nSo turn away from them! The day when the Caller calls to a dire thing,\nخُشَّعًا اَبْصَارُهُمْ يَخْرُجُوْنَ مِنَ الْاَجْدَاثِ كَاَنَّهُمْ جَرَادٌ مُّنْتَشِرٌۙ‏(7)\n\nthey will emerge from the graves as if they were scattered locusts with a humbled look [in their eyes],\nمُّهْطِعِيْنَ اِلَى الدَّاعِ‌ؕ يَقُوْلُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ هٰذَا يَوْمٌ عَسِرٌ‏(8)\n\nscrambling toward the summoner. The faithless will say, ‘This is a hard day!’\nكَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ فَكَذَّبُوْا عَبْدَنَا وَقَالُوْا مَجْنُوْنٌ وَّازْدُجِرَ‏(9)\n\nThe people of Noah impugned before them. So they impugned Our servant and said, ‘A crazy man,’ and he was reviled.\nفَدَعَا رَبَّهٗۤ اَنِّىْ مَغْلُوْبٌ فَانْتَصِرْ‏(10)\n\nThereat he invoked his Lord, [saying,] ‘I have been overcome, so help [me].’\nفَفَتَحْنَاۤ اَبْوَابَ السَّمَآءِ بِمَآءٍ مُّنْهَمِرٍ ۖ‏(11)\nFAFATAHNAA ABWAABAS SAMAAA-E BEMAAA-IM MUNHAMER.\nThen We opened the gates of the sky with pouring waters,\nوَّفَجَّرْنَا الْاَرْضَ عُيُوْنًا فَالْتَقَى الْمَآءُ عَلٰٓى اَمْرٍ قَدْ قُدِرَ‌ۚ‏(12)\nWA FAJJARNAL ARZA O’YOONAN FALTAQAL MAAA-O A’LAA AMRIN QAD QODER.\nand We made the earth burst forth with springs, and the waters met for a preordained purpose.\nوَحَمَلْنٰهُ عَلٰى ذَاتِ اَلْوَاحٍ وَّدُسُرٍۙ‏(13)\n\nWe bore him on a vessel made of planks and nails,\nتَجْرِىْ بِاَعْيُنِنَا‌ۚ جَزَآءً لِّمَنْ كَانَ كُفِرَ‏(14)\n\nwhich sailed [over the flood waters] in Our sight, as a retribution for him who was met with disbelief.\nوَلَقَدْ تَّرَكْنٰهَاۤ اٰيَةً فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(15)\n\nCertainly We have left it as a sign; so is there anyone who will be admonished?\nفَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(16)\n\nSo how were My punishment and warnings?\nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(17)\n\nCertainly We have made the Quran simple for the sake of admonishment. So is there anyone who will be admonished?\nكَذَّبَتْ عَادٌ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(18)\n\n[The people of] ‘Ad impugned [their apostle]. So how were My punishment and warnings?\nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِيْحًا صَرْصَرًا فِىْ يَوْمِ نَحْسٍ مُّسْتَمِرٍّۙ‏(19)\n\nIndeed We unleashed upon them an icy gale on an incessantly ill-fated day,\nتَنْزِعُ النَّاسَۙ كَاَنَّهُمْ اَعْجَازُ نَخْلٍ مُّنْقَعِرٍ‏(20)\n\nknocking down people as if they were trunks of uprooted palm trees.\nفَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(21)\n\nSo how were My punishment and warnings?!\nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(22)\n\nCertainly We have made the Quran simple for the sake of admonishment. So is there anyone who will be admonished?\nكَذَّبَتْ ثَمُوْدُ بِالنُّذُرِ‏(23)\n\n[The people of] Thamud denied the warnings,\nفَقَالُوْۤا اَبَشَرًا مِّنَّا وَاحِدًا نَّتَّبِعُهٗۤۙ اِنَّاۤ اِذًا لَّفِىْ ضَلٰلٍ وَّسُعُرٍ‏(24)\n\nand they said, ‘Are we to follow a lone human from ourselves?! Indeed then we would be in error and madness.’\nءَاُلْقِىَ الذِّكْرُ عَلَيْهِ مِنْۢ بَيْنِنَا بَلْ هُوَ كَذَّابٌ اَشِرٌ‏(25)\n\n‘Has the Reminder been cast upon him from among us? No, he is a self-conceited liar.’\nسَيَعْلَمُوْنَ غَدًا مَّنِ الْكَذَّابُ الْاَشِرُ‏(26)\n\n‘Tomorrow they will know who is a self-conceited liar.\nاِنَّا مُرْسِلُوا النَّاقَةِ فِتْنَةً لَّهُمْ فَارْتَقِبْهُمْ وَاصْطَبِرْ‏(27)\n\nWe are sending the She-camel as a trial for them; so watch them and be steadfast.\nوَنَبِّئْهُمْ اَنَّ الْمَآءَ قِسْمَةٌۢ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ۚ كُلُّ شِرْبٍ مُّحْتَضَرٌ‏(28)\n\nInform them that the water is to be shared between them; each of them showing up at his turn.’\nفَنَادَوْا صَاحِبَهُمْ فَتَعَاطٰى فَعَقَرَ‏(29)\n\nBut they called their companion, and he took [a knife] and hamstrung [her].\nفَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(30)\n\nSo how were My punishment and My warnings?!\nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ صَيْحَةً وَّاحِدَةً فَكَانُوْا كَهَشِيْمِ الْمُحْتَظِرِ‏(31)\n\nWe sent against them a single Cry, and they became like the dry sticks of a corral builder.\nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(32)\n\nCertainly We have made the Quran simple for the sake of admonishment. So is there anyone who will be admonished?\nكَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ لُوْطٍ ۢ بِالنُّذُرِ‏(33)\n\nAnd the people of Lot denied the warnings.\nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ حَاصِبًا اِلَّاۤ اٰلَ لُوْطٍ‌ؕ نَّجَّيْنٰهُمْ بِسَحَرٍۙ‏(34)\n\nWe unleashed upon them a rain of stones, excepting the family of Lot, whom We delivered at dawn\nنِّعْمَةً مِّنْ عِنْدِنَا‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِىْ مَنْ شَكَرَ‏(35)\n\nas a blessing from Us. Thus do We reward those who give thanks.\nوَلَقَدْ اَنْذَرَهُمْ بَطْشَتَنَا فَتَمَارَوْا بِالنُّذُرِ‏(36)\n\nHe had already warned them of Our punishment, but they disputed the warnings.\nوَلَقَدْ رَاوَدُوْهُ عَنْ ضَيْفِهٖ فَطَمَسْنَاۤ اَعْيُنَهُمْ فَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(37)\n\nThey even solicited of him his guests, whereat We blotted out their eyes, [saying,] ‘Taste My punishment and My warnings!’\nوَلَقَدْ صَبَّحَهُمْ بُكْرَةً عَذَابٌ مُّسْتَقِرٌّ‌ ۚ‏(38)\n\nEarly at dawn there visited them an abiding punishment:\nفَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(39)\n\n‘Taste My punishment and warnings!’\nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(40)\n\nCertainly We have made the Quran simple for the sake of admonishment. So is there anyone who will be admonished?\nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَ اٰلَ فِرْعَوْنَ النُّذُرُ‌ۚ‏(41)\n\nCertainly the warnings did come to Pharaoh’s clan\nكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا كُلِّهَا فَاَخَذْنٰهُمْ اَخْذَ عَزِيْزٍ مُّقْتَدِرٍ‏(42)\n\nwho denied all of Our signs. So We seized them with the seizing of One [who is] all-mighty, Omnipotent.\nاَكُفَّارُكُمْ خَيْرٌ مِّنْ اُولٰٓئِكُمْ اَمْ لَكُمْ بَرَآءَةٌ فِى الزُّبُرِ‌ۚ‏(43)\n\nAre your faithless better than those? Have you [been granted] [some sort of] immunity in the scriptures?\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ نَحْنُ جَمِيْعٌ مُّنْتَصِرٌ‏(44)\n\nDo they say, ‘We are a confederate league’?\nسَيُهْزَمُ الْجَمْعُ وَيُوَلُّوْنَ الدُّبُرَ‏(45)\n\nThe league will be routed and turn its back [to flee].\nبَلِ السَّاعَةُ مَوْعِدُهُمْ وَالسَّاعَةُ اَدْهٰى وَاَمَرُّ‏(46)\n\nIndeed, the Hour is their tryst; and the Hour will be most calamitous and bitter.\nاِنَّ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ وَّسُعُرٍ‌ۘ‏(47)\n\nIndeed the guilty are steeped in error and madness.\nيَوْمَ يُسْحَبُوْنَ فِى النَّارِ عَلٰى وُجُوْهِهِمْؕ ذُوْقُوْا مَسَّ سَقَرَ‏(48)\n\nThe day when they are dragged on their faces into the Fire, [it will be said to them,] ‘Taste the touch of hell!’\nاِنَّا كُلَّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقْنٰهُ بِقَدَرٍ‏(49)\n\nIndeed We have created everything in a measure,\nوَمَاۤ اَمْرُنَاۤ اِلَّا وَاحِدَةٌ كَلَمْحٍۢ بِالْبَصَرِ‏(50)\n\nand Our command is but a single [word], like the twinkling of an eye.\nوَلَقَدْ اَهْلَكْنَاۤ اَشْيَاعَكُمْ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(51)\n\nCertainly We have destroyed your likes. So is there anyone who will be admonished?\nوَكُلُّ شَىْءٍ فَعَلُوْهُ فِى الزُّبُرِ‏(52)\n\nEverything they have done is in the books,\nوَ كُلُّ صَغِيْرٍ وَّكَبِيْرٍ مُّسْتَطَرٌ‏(53)\n\nand everything big and small is committed to writing.\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّنَهَرٍۙ‏(54)\n\nIndeed the Godwary will be amid gardens and streams,\nفِىْ مَقْعَدِ صِدْقٍ عِنْدَ مَلِيْكٍ مُّقْتَدِرٍ‏(55)\n\nin the abode of truthfulness with an omnipotent King.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Qamar (The Moon)\nThis ’Makki’ Surah has 55 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the fact of the person who recites this Surah will shine like the full moon on the Day of Reckoning. The best time to recite this Surah is at night and this carries the highest reward.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that the one who recites this Surah will have a mount from Jannah on which he will sit when he wakes from his grave. Whoever keeps this Surah under his cap or turban at the time of Friday prayers will be highly respected by the people and his difficulties will be eased."
}
